void copy_bytes(char *dest, const char *src, size_t n) {
    // Loop through each byte and copy it from src to dest
    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        dest[i] = src[i];
    }
}
```
This function takes three arguments: `dest`, the destination memory location, `src`, the source memory location, and `n`, the number of bytes to copy. It loops through each byte in the range of `src` and copies it to the corresponding index in `dest`.

To use this function, you can call it with the appropriate arguments:
```
char buffer[10];
const char *str = "Hello";
